  "subdivision_of_building": "The proposals affect only a limited part of the building façade at ground-floor level. The works are confined to the installation of two external signage elements: a single projecting hanging sign fixed to the façade, and one wall-mounted plaque positioned adjacent to the main entrance. No other parts of the building are altered, and there are no changes to the building’s structure, layout, fabric, or internal areas. The remainder of the building, including upper floors and existing architectural features, will remain entirely unchanged.",
  "status": "Application Under Consideration",
  "description": "The proposed development comprises the installation of two discreet external signage elements associated with the existing ground-floor art gallery use, with no change of use proposed. The works include one projecting hanging sign and one wall-mounted plaque, both displaying the gallery name “BERNHEIM.” The hanging sign is modest in scale and designed to project from the façade at a high level, providing clear identification while maintaining a restrained visual presence within the street scene. The wall-mounted plaque is fixed flush to the façade at entrance level, offering a complementary and legible form of identification for visitors. Both signs are of a high-quality, minimal design, proportionate to the host building, and sympathetic to the architectural character of the property and surrounding conservation context. The proposed signage is intended to improve wayfinding and visibility for the gallery without resulting in visual clutter or harm to the amenity of the area.",
